{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466472",
      "title": "Understanding entryComponents",
      "lectureOrder": 641,
      "videoOrder": 590,
      "sourceHash": "e0d1222ddf551ef1d252a31bb179e48769ad294237b4baa5ece87ccc0fd3cb04",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Instructor: Well, we proceeded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "with rendering the component programmatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 9.33,
          "en": "but now when we tried to test it, we had this strange error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.33,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "And a quick side note here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 15.12,
          "en": "if you're not getting this error, if it just works for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.12,
          "end": 16.11,
          "en": "then this is the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.11,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "because you're using Angular 9 or higher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 21.12,
          "en": "This is simply a tiny change that was made",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.12,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "behind the scenes of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 25.02,
          "en": "So the general syntax and so on didn't change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.02,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "what I showed you works in all Angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 30.18,
          "en": "but in Angular 9 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.18,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "there was a behind the scenes change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "which makes this work out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 36.78,
          "en": "which of course is great, but if you are getting this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 38.16,
          "en": "which is also not unlikely,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 38.16,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "because not everyone is using the latest version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "well then here's why we get it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "It didn't find a component factory for alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "Well we created one here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 50.25,
          "en": "Why didn't it find that factory?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.25,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "Well ignore the first part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 53.79,
          "en": "This here is the interesting part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 53.79,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "Did you add it to NG module entry components?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.24,
          "en": "For this, you need to understand how Angular actually works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 60.24,
          "end": 63.42,
          "en": "behind the scenes when it comes to creating components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.42,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "Of course, any component, as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 69,
          "en": "as directives and pipes, you plan on working with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "you need to add them to your declarations array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 73.56,
          "en": "And we did this for the alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 73.56,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "We did this for all the components that were loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 78.06,
          "en": "This is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 78.06,
          "end": 80.43,
          "en": "for Angular to understand what's a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 80.43,
          "end": 82.23,
          "en": "or which components and directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 82.23,
          "end": 83.85,
          "en": "and all you have in your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 83.85,
          "end": 86.78999999999999,
          "en": "because it does not automatically scan all your files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 86.78999999999999,
          "end": 89.49,
          "en": "You need to tell it which components exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 89.49,
          "end": 93.06,
          "en": "Still, this alone only makes Angular aware of it so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 93.06,
          "end": 95.55,
          "en": "that it is able to create such a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "when it finds it in one of two places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 101.94,
          "en": "The first place would be in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 101.94,
          "end": 104.4,
          "en": "If in your templates, let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 104.4,
          "end": 109.17,
          "en": "of the recipe list component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "If it finds something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "like app recipe item like this selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "it basically looks into the declarations array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "finds it there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "and then is able to create that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.465,
          "en": "Great. The other place where Angular will look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 122.465,
          "end": 125.85,
          "en": "for this component is in your routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "In your route conflict.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 129.39,
          "en": "When you point at a component there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 132.327,
          "en": "Angular will also check that in the declarations array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 132.327,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "And if it finds it there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "it is able to create such a component and load it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 139.59,
          "en": "Now one place that does not work by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 139.59,
          "end": 142.32,
          "en": "is when you want to create a component manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 144.72,
          "en": "in code, which is the exact thing we're trying to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 146.25,
          "en": "in the off component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 146.25,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "There we're creating our own component factory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "with the alert component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 153.42000000000002,
          "en": "And now here Angular does not automatically reach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 153.42000000000002,
          "end": 155.22,
          "en": "out to the declarations array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 155.22,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "It simply doesn't do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 158.34,
          "en": "You can complain about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 158.34,
          "end": 160.23,
          "en": "Still it's the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "You instead deliberately need to inform Angular that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 166.77,
          "en": "in this case the alert component will need to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 168.66,
          "en": "be created at some place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "And that Angular basically should be prepared for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "It will prepare itself for this creation when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "it finds a component in the template or in a route conflict.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 179.94,
          "en": "But here it, it won't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 179.94,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "Now to tell Angular to be prepared for the creation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 187.14,
          "en": "of that component, you need to add a special property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 187.14,
          "end": 190.05,
          "en": "to the object you pass to NG module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 190.05,
          "end": 191.82,
          "en": "Besides declarations, imports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 191.82,
          "end": 194.85,
          "en": "and so on there is a property we haven't worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 194.85,
          "end": 198.24,
          "en": "with thus far, and that is entry components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 198.24,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "Entry components also is an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 203.67000000000002,
          "en": "and it's an array of component types but only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 203.67000000000002,
          "end": 207.72,
          "en": "of components that will eventually need to be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 211.14,
          "en": "without a selector or the route contact being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 211.14,
          "end": 213.36,
          "en": "So whenever a component is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 213.36,
          "end": 217.35,
          "en": "by selector, or you use it with the route configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 217.35,
          "end": 221.055,
          "en": "you don't need to add it here, which is why thus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 221.055,
          "end": 224.1,
          "en": "far we haven't added anything to entry components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 224.1,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "For alert component, it's differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 228.72,
          "en": "And there you simply need to add alert component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 228.72,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "to entry components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 231.36,
          "en": "Now one extra note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 231.36,
          "end": 233.7,
          "en": "about this entry component's property though depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 233.7,
          "end": 237,
          "en": "on the Angular version you're using, you might not need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 237,
          "end": 238.53,
          "en": "If you are working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 238.53,
          "end": 242.13,
          "en": "in a project that uses Angular 9 or higher",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "and you can check your package dot Jason file to find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 246.75,
          "en": "out which version you're using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 246.75,
          "end": 249.6,
          "en": "If you're in a project with Angular 9 or higher",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 249.6,
          "end": 251.76,
          "en": "you can omit entry components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 251.76,
          "end": 254.25,
          "en": "by default, because there Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 254.25,
          "end": 257.19,
          "en": "under the hood uses a different rendering engine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 257.19,
          "end": 258.75,
          "en": "It's name is Ivy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 258.75,
          "end": 261.3,
          "en": "and there it works differently under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 261.3,
          "end": 263.4,
          "en": "So the average syntax doesn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 263.4,
          "end": 266.4,
          "en": "The only difference is that you can omit entry components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 266.4,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "You don't have to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 269.88,
          "en": "specifying it there too isn't a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 269.88,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "You will never make an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 273.72,
          "en": "if you do specify entry components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 273.72,
          "end": 276.54,
          "en": "Just in some cases you could omit it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 276.54,
          "end": 279.12,
          "en": "Now Angular is ready to create that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 279.12,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "whenever you prompt it to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 285.03,
          "en": "and you do prompt it to create that component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 285.03,
          "end": 286.56,
          "en": "So now if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 286.56,
          "end": 288.42,
          "en": "after adding that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 288.42,
          "end": 290.31,
          "en": "to the entry components list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 290.31,
          "end": 294.33,
          "en": "and you try this again, you get your component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "And this is now created programmatically in code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 299.04,
          "en": "but of course it's not working correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 299.04,
          "end": 301.95,
          "en": "We can't dismiss it and we're all not seeing a message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 301.95,
          "end": 303.873,
          "en": "How can we make this work?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
